WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
The Great Barrier Reef covers
344,400 square kilometres,

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.710
and supports 77,000 full-time jobs.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.940
It was built by small animals.

4
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.850
Reef-building corals make
skeletons of calcium carbonate,

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.230
and together they build reefs.

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:24.150
That structure is habitat: shelter and
food for fish and many other species.

7
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.570
Now picture a farm far inland,
and a fishing boat out at sea.

8
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.910
How could either one push coral
species towards extinction?

9
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.530
In this mission, you'll trace how human
activity reaches reefs at three scales:

10
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.010
local, regional and global.

11
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.730
Then you'll find out the difference
between a species vanishing from one place,

12
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.170
and vanishing everywhere.

13
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:53.000
Your mission: explain how farming and fishing
can push coral species towards extinction.
